We cannot guarantee your safety, but I can promise you a startling experience.

00:48:07.800 --> 00:48:08.840
Yeah, we made two of them.

00:48:09.110 --> 00:48:13.720
The first one, fascinatingly, yeah, the first one was a big success.

00:48:13.880 --> 00:48:19.980
I think it was, it was in, I don't know if anybody knows about this, but if you get a

00:48:19.980 --> 00:48:23.680
piece of a picture, that means you get a tiny percentage of the profits.

00:48:24.430 --> 00:48:30.000
Film companies are notorious for being able to hide those profits for years and years and

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.210
years and you never get anything.

00:48:32.210 --> 00:48:35.580
Well, the money came in so fast on that first Dalek movie,

00:48:35.580 --> 00:48:37.690
they were in profit within the year,

00:48:37.690 --> 00:48:40.350
and they actually had to pay me money, which was wonderful.

00:48:40.350 --> 00:48:42.670
The second film, of course, wasn't as successful,

00:48:42.670 --> 00:48:44.630
despite the fact that 50,000 pounds

00:48:44.630 --> 00:48:46.490
had been spent on promoting it.

00:48:46.490 --> 00:48:48.530
And the idea, well, Spotsky's original plan

00:48:48.530 --> 00:48:52.000
to make a Dalek film every year was thereby scrapped.

00:48:52.000 --> 00:48:56.020
In later years, I did try to reduce their exposure

00:48:56.020 --> 00:49:00.000
by quite a lot, and also went on guarding the

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:02.800
Daleks throughout their history.

00:49:02.800 --> 00:49:06.060
My agent and I have guarded the Daleks tremendously.

00:49:06.060 --> 00:49:09.300
We've never allowed them to be used as figures of fun.

00:49:09.300 --> 00:49:12.700
We've never tried always to stop anybody looking inside

00:49:12.700 --> 00:49:16.210
them, stop them appearing on comedy shows,

00:49:16.210 --> 00:49:19.930
never use them in advertising, stuff like that,

00:49:19.930 --> 00:49:20.750
just to protect them.

00:49:20.750 --> 00:49:22.390
Because there was an image for those Daleks,

00:49:22.390 --> 00:49:24.010
and I didn't want that shattered.

00:49:24.010 --> 00:49:25.910
- Sabotsky never quite forgot his dream, though,

00:49:25.910 --> 00:49:27.700
of making a third "Doctor Who" film.

00:49:27.700 --> 00:49:30.000
And around the early '80s was planning something called "Doctor

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:33.500
greatest adventure, which by all accounts would have been a Doctor Who and Jurassic

00:49:33.500 --> 00:49:36.490
Park type film, 15 years ahead of its time.

00:49:36.490 --> 00:49:56.540
Well, for a long time I just simply liked Daleks and Doctor Who, and built lots of

00:49:56.540 --> 00:50:00.000
little models and things, like a lot of kids would be.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:05.490
do and gradually that becomes not quite enough you want to go a little bit

00:50:05.490 --> 00:50:12.630
further do something else so it was in a case of what can we do to sort of

00:50:12.630 --> 00:50:22.630
animate them in some way so yeah why not do a film and really it was in essence

00:50:22.630 --> 00:50:30.000
supposed to be the third Dalek film well this little chap here is

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:39.610
is roughly about two foot tall, and initially the hardest bid on the Dalek or any Dalek

00:50:39.610 --> 00:50:46.780
is getting loads of these little hemispheres. So because I didn't have much money, I thought

00:50:46.780 --> 00:50:50.140
well the cheapest thing to do is to get lots of little ping pong balls, cut them all in

00:50:50.140 --> 00:50:56.440
half and scale it up from there. So that's really the reason why they're the size that

00:50:56.440 --> 00:51:00.000
they are. Gradually as I got further and further into

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:04.740
to it, I decided to try and make the thing bigger and better. And I think at one point

00:51:04.740 --> 00:51:12.060
I even built about 20 Daleks of that size, because I wanted it to go a little bit better

00:51:12.060 --> 00:51:16.940
than they had in the films, keep that sort of spectacle, but try and improve on it if

00:51:16.940 --> 00:51:17.560
it was possible.

00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:25.060
I think one shouldn't underestimate the popularity of the Daleks now, never mind during the 60s

00:51:25.060 --> 00:51:30.000
when they were, of course, huge. Even as recently as last year, Marvel,

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:35.480
were able to successfully reprint the old, very popular Dalek comic strips

00:51:35.480 --> 00:51:39.780
from TV21 comic, and indeed the American comic strip adaptation

00:51:39.780 --> 00:51:44.100
of the first film, which hadn't been available in this country to that point.

00:51:44.470 --> 00:51:47.230
I would like to draw your attention to this picture,

00:51:47.580 --> 00:51:51.700
because that is a picture in a cartoon magazine of Yvonne here

00:51:51.700 --> 00:51:54.110
and of myself here.

00:51:54.770 --> 00:51:58.930
And as Yvonne has just pointed out, we both looked as though we were dreaming,

00:51:59.130 --> 00:52:00.000
We were space people.

00:52:00.250 --> 00:52:07.130
in our maiden form bras and there we are, rather flattering and I must say I look as

00:52:07.130 --> 00:52:12.590
if I'm more in need of a bra than anybody else you've seen in that. But there we are.

00:52:12.590 --> 00:52:19.860
So I want, I'm utterly thrilled that I am in a comic. I really think it's absolutely

00:52:19.860 --> 00:52:21.130
wonderful.

00:52:21.130 --> 00:52:30.000
I've kept some souvenirs from the films. I've got my two film scripts and I've also got something from the

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:38.110
to Gordon Fleming. We had a small deal going on the side of this filming. If I did a shot

00:52:38.110 --> 00:52:45.070
in one take, he would give me a shilling, he told me. So we went through the whole filming

00:52:45.070 --> 00:52:53.050
and every time I did a take in one, he said, "That's right, I owe you another shilling."

00:52:53.050 --> 00:52:56.610
So I wasn't really sure about this at the time or whether it was something he was just

00:52:56.610 --> 00:53:00.000
saying to me. But on the last day of filming,

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:04.940
we'd finished and he called me over and he said I've got something for you and I

00:53:04.940 --> 00:53:13.370
said oh and he he gave me this little bag and it says to one take Tovey love

00:53:13.370 --> 00:53:20.650
Gordon and inside are 21 shillings so I must have done 21 takes for him in one

00:53:20.650 --> 00:53:26.480
one go so that was quite good we didn't do it on the second movie I think perhaps

00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:30.000
it must have cost him too much money I think he must have realized then I could do

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:36.780
it in one take so we didn't do it but I still have it and I've I treasure it people always ask

00:53:36.780 --> 00:53:41.810
me if they can if they can come and see the movie they know I've got a copy and I mean it's boring

00:53:41.810 --> 00:53:47.480
for me I'm usually mixing tea or something I've seen it so many times but everybody loves it

00:53:47.480 --> 00:53:52.500
everybody loves the Daleks I mean there was no nowhere further to go if you'd work with a Dalek

00:53:52.500 --> 00:53:58.570
that's just it the films are are so big and colorful and exciting I think any child of any

00:53:58.570 --> 00:54:00.000
generation watching them.

00:54:00.160 --> 00:54:04.520
we'll still find a thrill from them because the adventure is so broad.

00:54:04.520 --> 00:54:08.020
They have a very good story, they're very exciting,

00:54:08.020 --> 00:54:10.340
they're very well told and well presented.

00:54:10.340 --> 00:54:14.240
I don't think you need to know an awful lot about Doctor Who to enjoy them.

00:54:14.240 --> 00:54:16.900
They stand up on their own as a very good product.

00:54:16.900 --> 00:54:19.800
But Daleks in particular had an appeal

00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:23.220
which is a bit difficult to explain to people that

00:54:23.220 --> 00:54:26.390
can't see the reason why you like them so much.

00:54:26.390 --> 00:54:30.000
But they're a fairly unique design, I mean there's nothing that's

00:54:30.220 --> 00:54:39.020
quite looks like a dalek i mean a child can make a a a toy or a or a drawing of a dalek and although

00:54:39.020 --> 00:54:44.040
it's nowhere is it going to be accurate you know exactly what it's meant to be so it's a very unique

00:54:44.040 --> 00:54:52.770
thing many kids grew up watching they would not miss it for anything but they'd watch from outside

00:54:52.770 --> 00:54:59.350
the room through a crack in the door or from behind the couch it frightened them but they wouldn't

00:55:00.160 --> 00:55:04.410
